  "music": "w1-doodle-docks",
  "authorNotes": "Solo. The set piece: a cargo crane you climb rather than swing past, built as three successive platformMoving 'boom' segments (crane-boom-1/2/3) that each drift once (loop: false) along a short rising path and then hold at the end — climbed back-to-back this is a ~40s continuous ascent, and each segment's static angle (0, 0.17, 0.35 rad — roughly 0, 10, 20 degrees) steps up the higher you climb, so the structure reads as increasingly tilted by the time you reach the top (~30 degrees total, matching the design brief). Note for whoever wires this to the engine: `Prop.angle` is a single static value with no time-animated rotation field in the current contract, so this is a translate-and-step approximation of 'the crane tips as you climb it', not a literally continuously-rotating rigid body — a real animated-tilt prop kind would need a schema addition, which is out of this ticket's scope (types.ts is not mine to edit). The checkpoint sits at boom-1's landing so a fall partway up doesn't send you back to the dock. camera-9 is picked up at spawn for the photo objective (allAirborne) — easiest to trigger stepping between boom segments. A short assist beam bridges the base and the final gap into the goal platform for players who'd rather not trust the last rung."
